# hirely Project Conventions

## Stack

- Next.js
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS

## General Principles

- Write clear, maintainable, and readable code.
- Prefer simple solutions over unnecessary abstractions.
- Use TypeScript properly; avoid `any` unless there is a justified reason.
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Follow the existing project structure and conventions before introducing new patterns.
- Do not add dependencies unless they provide clear value.
- Keep accessibility in mind when building UI components.

## React / Next.js

- Prefer functional React components.
- Use Server Components by default where appropriate.
- Use Client Components only when client-side interactivity or browser APIs require them.
- Keep business logic separate from presentation where practical.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Prefer reusable utility patterns over large custom CSS files.
- Maintain consistent spacing, typography, and responsive behavior.

## AI-Assisted Development

- Explain significant implementation decisions when asked.
- Before making large changes, inspect the existing code and understand its structure.
- Do not rewrite working code unnecessarily.
- When requirements are ambiguous, identify the ambiguity instead of inventing requirements.